# Git branch workflow

- Never commit feature work directly on `main`.
- Start (or switch to) a `dev` / feature branch before making changes.
- Prefer names like `dev`, `dev/<topic>`, or `feature/<topic>`.
- When the work is complete and the user asks to ship it: merge (or open a PR) into `main`, then push.
- Do not push unfinished work to `main` unless the user explicitly says to.
